data.content:
It works. Here's the full program:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```

**Output:**
```json
{"Name":"Alice","Age":30}
```

`JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` is a built-in policy that converts property names to PascalCase. Since your record uses lowercase parameter names (`name`, `age`), the generated properties are also lowercase — the policy converts them to `Name` and `Age` in the JSON output.
